--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Accidental limit state: IEA-15MW VolturnUS-S on three chains, line 1 breaks at the fairlead at 3.0 MN
-- The floating system (hull, ballast, tower and rotor-nacelle assembly) is one free Rigid6 body.
-- Mass, centre of gravity, inertias, displacement and waterplane stiffness come from the OpenFAST
-- IEA-15MW UMaine VolturnUS-S model; the reference point is the system centre of gravity, 3.34 m
-- below the still-water line, and C44/C55 act about it. Ca is the WAMIT zero-frequency surge
-- added mass. CdA = 1000 m^2 and the EXTERNAL LOADS linear damping, which stands in for radiation
-- and viscous damping, are assumptions. The lumped body has no wave drift force: use it to screen
-- a line failure, and the coupled OpenFAST route for design.
-- A constant 2 MN force toward azimuth 60 deg stands in for the mean rotor thrust, and the
-- JONSWAP sea (Hs 6 m, Tp 11 s) travels the same way, so line 3 is the windward line. Line 1 is
-- taken as weakened: it detaches from its fairlead the first time its fairlead tension reaches
-- 3.0 MN (FAILURE FailTen). Otherwise this deck is als_volturnus_line_break_time.dat.
